  5901                                  ; ahci_mark_uncached: edi = a physical address inside the 2MB page to mark
  5902                                  ; uncached (sets PCD, bit4) in the identity-map PDs built by
  5903                                  ; expand_identity_map (4 contiguous page directories at 0x3000..0x6FFF,
  5904                                  ; 512 entries each, 2MB pages). Without this, polling an HBA register
  5905                                  ; through a cacheable mapping could read back a stale value instead of
  5906                                  ; what the device just wrote - the ABAR sits in a dedicated MMIO range
  5907                                  ; that nothing else in this kernel uses, so marking its whole 2MB page
  5908                                  ; uncached doesn't affect anything else.
